      "type": "multiple-choice",
      "difficulty": "knowledge-check",
      "stem": "Two sequences have nth terms $5n - 3$ and $2n + 15$. At which term are they equal?",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "a",
          "text": "$n = 4$"
        },
        {
          "id": "b",
          "text": "$n = 6$"
        },
        {
          "id": "c",
          "text": "$n = 5$"
        },
        {
          "id": "d",
          "text": "$n = 12$"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "b",
      "explanation": "Set equal: $5n - 3 = 2n + 15$, so $3n = 18$, $n = 6$. At $n = 6$, both sequences give $5(6) - 3 = 27$."
